  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a black man running away from police officers in a confrontational street scene, overlaid with the text 'do you have any idea how black you were going'. This juxtaposition uses a racially charged metaphor, implying the man's skin color is so dark that it is literally 'black' in a derogatory, stereotypical way. This directly invokes anti-Black racism by equating dark skin with criminality or danger, reinforcing harmful stereotypes that associate Blackness with aggression or criminal behavior. The meme's intent is to demean and dehumanize Black individuals by reducing their identity to a racialized, negative caricature, making it a hateful and toxic piece of content.",
